{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 10, :comments ["<b>Woe.</b> Or it means: Can a son say to his father, before he is born, \"What will you beget?\" and to the woman who is his mother, \"What will you labor with?\" — as in \"For Zion labored and bore\" (Isaiah 66:8)."], :book :isaiah, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 45, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Isaiah, by M. Friedlander; Society of Hebrew Literature, London 1877" "https://www.nli.org.il/he/books/NNL_ALEPH001338443"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:58:07.120154123Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}